# index.html is generated by `study build` from everything under courses/.
#
# Git's textual three-way merge is actively harmful on generated output: it
# splices two builds together and the result looks healthy while being wrong.
# That has already happened once — the newer half supplied the app code so the
# page rendered normally, while the older half supplied a stale data payload,
# so a whole feature silently showed as empty.
#
# `-merge` stops git attempting it. On a conflict the file is left whole and
# flagged, and the resolution is always the same, because the file is entirely
# derived:
#
#     study build && git add index.html
#
index.html -merge
